- **The sync — this fork's ninth upstream take, by the take the founder chooses at P4.** After `git fetch upstream` (2026-11-01T15:27Z), `upstream/main` (DioxusLabs/blitz) reads `e42ee1f25` ("Fix off-screen culling bounds applying node location twice (#1342)", committed 2026-10-30T16:25:16Z). The merge base is still `23b9b26a9`. `git rev-list` counts 57 upstream commits not in HEAD and 186 of ours not upstream. Twenty-four of the 57 are already in as cherry-picks, by the `(cherry picked from commit …)` trailers on our branch, 24 trailers and none naming a commit outside the range (scratch read over `git log --format=%B 23b9b26a9..HEAD`; `git cherry` cannot count them, a conflict-resolved pick changes its patch id). **That leaves 33 commits to take or leave:**
  - **left out at the last take, sixteen** (the first freight block below): six Taffy-main commits (`1a11761bc` · `4a5ab9cc9` · `510b592ab` · `1e5479ae6` · `b8f4ba6fd` · `9babd796a`), `06ecec886` (git Stylo 0.23-pre) with `3954ecb85` and `1c5265a8b`, `286874cc1` (Dioxus 0.8.0-alpha.3), `a09f46792` · `527394724` (winit beta.4, its clipboard API in place of `arboard`), `d3ed4e2c7` · `ccfe15332` (git Taffy), `0980cce5f` (reversed scroll origins through Taffy's `ScrollableOverflow`) and `ebacd68bd` (hit testing with no computed styles yet);
  - **new since `ebacd68bd`, seventeen:**
    - pins: `0674e8efa` and `784a567e4` (git Stylo `de0f23c`, then `cd230184a`), and `e5929f9e2`, which names manifests beside its engine lines (`-webkit-text-fill-color`);
    - engine code: `fe33b778b` (#1276, narrower restyle invalidation on DOM mutation, 909 lines added), `8b1a0a3ce` (#1312, layout damage for SVG attributes and `<col span>`), `dee854c76` (#1317, `<picture>`'s UA rule), `f6edb9701` (#1318, a failed stylesheet no longer blocks rendering), `6fca6308d` (#1316, `mix-blend-mode` and `isolation`), `7a3dd8918` (#1310, Stylo preferences before the UA sheet), `a26c6ddeb` (#1322, `CustomWidget` attributes replayed), `f76777766` (#1319, inline box decorations), `6ef4b532d` (#1305, no mounted event for an element removed in the same render), `ae774d7f4` (#1339, unrounded layout for computed sizes), `ac6f9f582` (#1340, `background-clip: text`), `e42ee1f25` (#1342, off-screen culling bounds);
    - script: `91ef65e21` (#1314, `URLSearchParams`);
    - upstream-only surface: `22f0cd000` (#1337, `AGENTS.md`).

- **The take is a fork, decided at P4.** The precedent is the founder's own word at the last two syncs: «Десять коммитов (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-24) and «Одиннадцать коммитов (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-27, `chunks/2026-10-27-upstream-sync-engine-debts/inputs/I4-upstream-sync-epoch2-founder-2026-10-27.md.txt`), each a cherry-pick with the pins unchanged; passed over at the last were «Одиннадцать + winit beta.4», «Весь мердж» and «Ничего не брать». The recorded rule is "no git dependency is left in the root manifest … keep both" (`.claude/rules/security.md` §Dependencies), together with the coupled pins (CLAUDE.md Critical Warnings). Upstream's manifest at `e42ee1f25` names git Stylo (`version = "0.22.0"`, `nicoburns/stylo` rev `78734bf5…`), git Taffy `c2560562…`, Dioxus `0.8.0-alpha.3` and winit `=0.31.0-beta.4`; ours names stylo 0.22.0, taffy 0.15, Dioxus 0.7.3 and winit `=0.31.0-beta.3`. P3 measures the candidate shapes, each a measured fact, on a trial worktree [inferred]:
  - cherry-pick, onto the registry pins, the new commits that build without git Taffy, git Stylo or Dioxus 0.8 — the founder's last two shapes. Which of the seventeen build so is P3's reading, commit by commit;
  - that take plus winit beta.4 (`a09f46792`, `527394724`): a registry pin moved inside upstream's own coupled set, so no git dependency, but "pins unchanged" no longer holds — passed over by him at the last sync, measured green there;
  - merge `upstream/main` (`e42ee1f25`) whole: git dependencies and a Dioxus alpha in the root manifest and the stable-id port. It reverses his rule, so it is his fork. The entry's own hint says "merged", and whether that wording is the take or a shape among them is his, not a reading;
  - take nothing, leaving the whole delta to the next sync.
  Whatever is chosen, the pin is a measured sha. If `upstream/main` moves before /implement, the chunk still targets the measured sha, and later commits go to the next sync. Moving the pin is the operator's call.

